1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,503
So we have two ways of looking at math, we have

2
00:00:03,603 --> 00:00:08,948
the computational world of syntax, and the platonic world of semantics.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,907
To understand the relation between these two worlds, let's start with

4
00:00:14,007 --> 00:00:18,044
a simple language with a single binary relation symbol E.

5
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:21,129
We can visualize models in this language by

6
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:24,513
sets of points and arrows between these points.

7
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,140
We need to define axioms to determine

8
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:31,852
the behaviour of this edge relation E.

9
00:00:31,933 --> 00:00:37,507
Without any axioms, every possible combination of points and all possible

10
00:00:37,607 --> 00:00:41,937
arrows drawn between them is a model of our empty theory.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,332
An axiom can be any FOL sentence.

12
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,882
For example, we can consider

13
00:00:47,982 --> 00:00:51,756
this formula phi, expressing transitivity,

14
00:00:51,866 --> 00:00:55,258
meaning that if there is some path between nodes,

15
00:00:55,358 --> 00:00:58,678
then there is a direct path between these nodes,

16
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:05,058
or this sentence psi expressing irreflexitivity, which enforces that any

17
00:01:05,158 --> 00:01:09,300
model of it must not contain any self-referential arrows.

18
00:01:09,466 --> 00:01:11,779
Such sentences are true in some of

19
00:01:11,879 --> 00:01:14,334
the structures, and false in others.

20
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:18,816
We can combine the sentences, and consider the collection of

21
00:01:18,916 --> 00:01:23,182
all structures which satisfy both phi and psi for example,

22
00:01:23,282 --> 00:01:28,076
i.e. the collection of all transitive and irreflexive structures.

23
00:01:28,133 --> 00:01:32,305
We will denote this collection by the model set of phi and psi.

24
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:36,489
If we start to analyze the structures in this collection, we

25
00:01:36,589 --> 00:01:39,980
might notice some things in common to all of them.

26
00:01:40,066 --> 00:01:43,684
For example we may notice that in none of them do we

27
00:01:43,784 --> 00:01:46,686
have an arrow from a to b and from b to a.

28
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:51,278
We can easily see why, since if we did have an edge from a

29
00:01:51,378 --> 00:01:56,252
to b and from b to a in a transitive and irreflexive structure,

30
00:01:56,333 --> 00:02:00,865
then by transitivity we should have a direct path a to a.

31
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,268
But then the structures is not irreflexive, a contradiction.

32
00:02:06,466 --> 00:02:08,673
So, we see that adding this

33
00:02:08,773 --> 00:02:12,774
sentence chi expressing assymetry, is redundant,

34
00:02:12,866 --> 00:02:19,918
in the sense that Mod(phi,psi,chi)=Mod(phi,psi).

35
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,812
We denote this by {phi,psi} models chi.

